 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Use several bags of ice, then throw them out and replace them every couple of hours. Try to keep them in a sealed plastic bag. Ice cubes work too, but bags of ice last longer and keep things colder. Keep the cooler in a shaded spot and try to keep the lid on as much as possible. And bring it indoors on the hot days. Ask him to leave it alone while you' away. A cool spot to sit while you pack and unpack helps too. Yes, definitely. Freeze it in ice cube trays before you leave, then you' got cold water waiting when you get back.",
